title: What the week actually created
subtitle: week-12-detections-as-code — terraform state after apply, 7 resources
width: 1000
---
$ terraform state list
azurerm_log_analytics_workspace.detections
azurerm_monitor_diagnostic_setting.activity
azurerm_resource_group.detections
azurerm_sentinel_alert_rule_scheduled.escalation
azurerm_sentinel_alert_rule_scheduled.tampering
azurerm_sentinel_automation_rule.tag_escalation
azurerm_sentinel_log_analytics_workspace_onboarding.detections

$ terraform output
  resource_group         = rg-detections-lab-dev-scus-001
  workspace_name         = law-wk12-dev-scus-001
  detection_rule_names   = ["Role assignment created", "Policy assignment deleted"]

# Sentinel is ENABLED on a workspace, not deployed. The onboarding and
# the workspace are separate objects with separate lifecycles, which is
# why removing Sentinel does not remove the workspace -- or its bill.
